		const jokeList = [
			"Why did the chicken cross the road?",
			"Why did the scarecrow win an award?",
			"Why did the bicycle fall over?",
			"Why did the computer beep?",
		];

		const jokeButton = document.getElementById("joke-button");
		jokeButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
			const jokeContainer = document.getElementById("joke-container");
			jokeContainer.innerHTML = jokeList[Math.floor(Math.random() * jokeList.length)];
		});
	</script>
</body>
</html>
```
In this example, the HTML code defines a simple webpage with a heading, a button, and a container for the jokes. The JavaScript code defines a list of jokes and an event listener that listens for clicks on the button. When the button is clicked, the JavaScript code randomly selects a joke from the list and sets the content of the joke container to the selected joke.
